{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh: the second decision that was never actually addressed to you. Claude found that GIT_COMMON_DIR (and the wider ambient git-env family — GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL/SYSTEM, HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME) can redirect gitstore object reads and carry executable git config, despite the --git-dir pin. The fix is scoped and ready (request d2605fd7, held by claude), but it waits on one ruling only you can give: is the operator's ambient environment inside the threat model? If yes, hermeticGitEnvironment should strip the whole hostile family (routing GIT_DIR/WORK_TREE/COMMON_DIR plus config GIT_CONFIG_*), not just the config subset. If no, we document the assumption and close the finding. Three env-family holes have surfaced this way, so the ruling settles a class, not one bug. Rule in or out; either answer unblocks claude.","body":{"conditions":"Rule whether the operator's ambient git environment (GIT_COMMON_DIR, GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL/SYSTEM, HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME) is inside gitseq's threat model. If in-scope: authorize claude to extend hermeticGitEnvironment to strip the whole routing+config family, closing request d2605fd7. If out-of-scope: state the trust assumption for the record so d2605fd7 can be closed as documented-not-defended. Either ruling is an admissible closer for the finding.","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"}}